# Suricata rules - BTCPay Server Greenfield API TOTP 2FA bypass (PR #7491, fixed in v2.4.2)
# Author: al4n4n (Dadb0d)
#
# CWE-287 Authentication Bypass. The vulnerable BasicAuthenticationHandler accepted HTTP
# Basic auth (email:password) for an account whose second factor is TOTP, because it only
# rejected accounts that had a FIDO2 credential (user.Fido2Credentials.Any()). These rules
# surface HTTP Basic authentication against the Greenfield API, which is the on-the-wire
# signature of the bypass (and, after the fix, of attempts that the server now rejects).
#
# NOTE: BTCPay is normally deployed behind TLS. These rules match cleartext HTTP, so they
# fire on a TLS-terminating proxy's plaintext leg, on an internal HTTP listener, or against
# the shipped capture/exploit.pcap. See capture/README.md for the test command.
#
# Local SID range 9100000-9100099.

# 1) Any HTTP Basic auth to a Greenfield API path. Post-fix (v2.4.2) Basic auth to the API
#    is disabled by default 5 minutes after account creation (PR #7492), so this is anomalous.
alert http any any -> any any ( \
    msg:"BTCPAY Greenfield API HTTP Basic authentication (possible TOTP 2FA bypass PR#7491)"; \
    flow:established,to_server; \
    http.uri; content:"/api/v1/"; startswith; \
    http.header; content:"Authorization|3a 20|Basic "; nocase; \
    classtype:attempted-admin; \
    reference:url,github.com/btcpayserver/btcpayserver/pull/7491; \
    metadata:cwe CWE-287, affected_version 2.4.1, fixed_version 2.4.2; \
    sid:9100001; rev:1;)

# 2) Higher fidelity: Basic auth aimed at server-admin / fund-bearing endpoints
#    (user list, server info, store + Lightning node data) = post-bypass enumeration.
alert http any any -> any any ( \
    msg:"BTCPAY Greenfield API Basic auth to sensitive endpoint (post-2FA-bypass enumeration)"; \
    flow:established,to_server; \
    http.uri; content:"/api/v1/"; startswith; \
    pcre:"/^\/api\/v1\/(users|server|stores)/i"; \
    http.header; content:"Authorization|3a 20|Basic "; nocase; \
    classtype:attempted-admin; \
    reference:url,github.com/btcpayserver/btcpayserver/pull/7491; \
    metadata:cwe CWE-287, affected_version 2.4.1, fixed_version 2.4.2; \
    sid:9100002; rev:1;)

# 3) Response-side: a patched server (v2.4.2+) rejects the bypass with this exact message.
#    Seeing it means someone is actively trying the 2FA bypass against a patched instance.
alert http any any -> any any ( \
    msg:"BTCPAY Greenfield API 2FA bypass attempt blocked by patched handler"; \
    flow:established,to_client; \
    file.data; content:"Cannot use Basic authentication when multi-factor is enabled"; nocase; \
    classtype:attempted-admin; \
    reference:url,github.com/btcpayserver/btcpayserver/pull/7491; \
    metadata:cwe CWE-287, fixed_version 2.4.2; \
    sid:9100003; rev:1;)
